      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has many issues hurting understandability:\n1. Massive block of unused imports\n2. Five unused class-level constants (`YEAR_STANDARD`, `YEAR_LEAP`, `STANDARD_YEAR_LENGTH`, `TEST`, `PARIS`)\n3. Magic literal `2008` appearing twice with no named constant\n4. Noisy `//-----...` section separators\n\nI'll write an improved version that cleans all of this up while keeping all three test methods identical in behavior.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored file removes all unused imports and dead constants (`YEAR_STANDARD`, `YEAR_LEAP`, `STANDARD_YEAR_LENGTH`, `TEST`, `PARIS`), introduces a named `LEAP_YEAR = 2008` constant to eliminate the repeated magic literal, and strips the noisy section-separator comments — all while keeping the three test methods and their runtime behaviour identical."
